<!--
  MachineBlocks — SCAD documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.MbBlockApi
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <name>MbBlockApi</name>
  <type>scad:MbBlockApi</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to the mb_block() public API</is>

  <documentation>
    mb_block() is the single public native geometry module of the MachineBlocks V3 SCAD library.
    All printable leaf geometry goes through it — complexity is parameters, composition, and nesting.

    Public signature:
    mb_block(config = undef, settings = undef)

    config and settings are optional arrays of [key, value] pairs (pseudo-maps). Resolution order
    for each parameter: settings → config → default. Merge helpers combine layers; never read the
    arrays by hand inside Block Modules.

    Native parameters use dedicated getters mb_param_* (config, settings, optional default).
    Custom (non-native) parameters use mb_param(config, settings, name, default).

    config carries environment, calibration, and shared profile values. settings carry instance
    overrides for one call. Calibration adjustments belong in config profiles — not as routine
    settings on content blocks.

    Parameter inventory, types, defaults, and documentation are defined on
    com.machineblocks.bml.core.NativeBlock — that Block is the SSOT. SCAD docs explain the call
    model; they do not redefine the parameter set.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="scad:BlockFileStructure" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — mandatory Block File section layout.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:NativeBlock" relation="Defines">
      SSOT for every native mb_block() parameter.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
